# Test: OSPF fast-reroute (LFA / TI-LFA) configuration acceptance and wiring.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-ospf-ext-6 -- the `fast-reroute { enable; mode; node-protection }`
# YANG container is accepted, resolved into the engine config, inherited into the
# OSPFv3 address family, and threaded into the SPF Computer so enabling it runs the
# LFA pass in Run.
# PREVENTS: fast-reroute config being silently dropped or not reaching the Computer.
#
# Live FRR/QEMU kernel failover is owned by the ospf-lfa-frr interop scenario.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=go test -v ./internal/plugins/ospf ./internal/plugins/ospf/spf -run TestFastReroute(ConfigParse|DisabledByDefault|ModeDefaultsToLFA|ConfigEnablesLFAPass|DisabledNoBackup)$ -count=1:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=TestFastRerouteConfigParse
expect=stdout:contains=TestFastRerouteDisabledByDefault
expect=stdout:contains=TestFastRerouteModeDefaultsToLFA
expect=stdout:contains=TestFastRerouteConfigEnablesLFAPass
expect=stdout:contains=TestFastRerouteDisabledNoBackup
